  "content": {
    "id": "p52-q85-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x^2+3x-5$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p52-q85-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the range of $f$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left[-\\dfrac{29}{4},\\infty\\right)$.\n\nCompleting the square gives the minimum value $-\\dfrac{29}{4}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\left(x+\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{9}{4}-5\\\\f(x)&=\\left(x+\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{29}{4}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe squared term is nonnegative and equals zero when $x=-\\dfrac{3}{2}$, so the minimum value is $-\\dfrac{29}{4}$. The range is $\\left[-\\dfrac{29}{4},\\infty\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-q85-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $f(2)$ and $f(-3)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(2)=5$, $f(-3)=-5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(2)&=2^2+3(2)-5\\\\f(2)&=5\\\\f(-3)&=(-3)^2+3(-3)-5\\\\f(-3)&=-5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-q85-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find $a$ such that $f(a)=13$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=3$ or $a=-6$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a^2+3a-5&=13\\\\a^2+3a-18&=0\\\\(a-3)(a+6)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ or $a=-6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
